{"w": 595.3200073242188, "h": 809.0257568359375, "lines": [{"t": "22", "x": 0.9048578681186661, "y": 0.9742087522985531, "w": 0.028885380484969688, "h": 0.017428414981790374, "c": 1, "size": 12.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "became hyper-vigilant to bad news, even when it had nothing to do with their job", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.12319506908974809, "w": 0.8267684298600647, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "(such as learning that the likelihood of card fraud was higher than they'd thought),", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.15152541916388573, "w": 0.8260335309911918, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "and altered their beliefs in response. In contrast, stress didn't change how they", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.17970752416545568, "w": 0.8259030167249982, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "responded to good news (such as learning that the likelihood of card fraud was", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.2080378742395933, "w": 0.8260117957009852, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "lower than they'd thought).", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.23636822431373095, "w": 0.2798751563890014, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Back in our lab, we observed the same pattern in students who were told they had", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.26469857438786853, "w": 0.8260120007508928, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "to give a surprise public speech, which would be judged by a panel, recorded and", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.2930660423122369, "w": 0.8260988393867654, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "posted online. Sure enough, their cortisol levels spiked, their heart rates went up", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.32139637352567824, "w": 0.8267989822962986, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "and they suddenly became better at processing unrelated, yet alarming,", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.3497267990426009, "w": 0.8259682225956181, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "information about rates of disease and violence.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.3780571491167385, "w": 0.49135809475007647, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "When we experience stressful events, a physiological change is triggered that", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.40638753691226864, "w": 0.8259030167249982, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "causes us to take in warnings and focus on what might go wrong. Brain imaging", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.4347178869864063, "w": 0.8264461939302562, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "reveals that this 'switch' is related to a sudden boost in a neural signal important", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.4630482747819364, "w": 0.825837503279517, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "for learning, specifically in response to unexpected warning signs, such as faces", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.49140337008956114, "w": 0.8259681200706643, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "expressing fear.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5197337201636988, "w": 0.16936314984544876, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Such neural engineering could have helped prehistoric humans to survive. When", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5480641079592289, "w": 0.8263792451354216, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "our ancestors found themselves surrounded by hungry animals, they would have", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5763944580333665, "w": 0.8261204721520182, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "benefited from an increased ability to learn about hazards. In a safe environment,", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6047248458288966, "w": 0.8261642503072929, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "however, it would have been wasteful to be on high alert constantly. So, a neural", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6330551959030343, "w": 0.8265422598119713, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "switch that automatically increases or decreases our ability to process warnings", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6612743433120499, "w": 0.8261425150170862, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "in response to changes in our environment could have been useful. In fact, people", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6896046933861876, "w": 0.8261862931723609, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "with clinical depression and anxiety seem unable to switch away from a state in", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.7179351189031102, "w": 0.8266094136567135, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "which they absorb all the negative messages around them.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.7462654689772478, "w": 0.6004590503544134, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "It is also important to realise that stress travels rapidly from one person to the", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.7745958190513854, "w": 0.8260120007508928, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "next. If a co-worker is stressed, we are more likely to tense up and feel stressed", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8029261691255231, "w": 0.8260302501926701, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "ourselves. We don't even need to be in the same room with someone for their", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8312565191996607, "w": 0.8259912907102241, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "emotions to influence our behaviour. Studies show that if we observe positive", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8596116899500704, "w": 0.8259681200706643, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "feeds on social media, such as images of a pink sunset, we are more likely to post", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8879420400242081, "w": 0.8261424124921325, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}], "source": "pdf text layer"}